msgid ""
"Visit the <a href=\"https://forum.newsblur.com\">NewsBlur support forum</a> to ask questions, report "
"problems, or suggest features."
msgstr ""
"Visitez le <a href=\"https://forum.newsblur.com\">NewsBlur forum d’assistance</a> pour poser vos questions,"
" signaler des problèmes ou suggérer des fonctionnalités."

msgid "Visit the forum"
msgstr "Visiter le forum"

msgid "Visual Training (Thumbs Up/Down)"
msgstr "Entraînement visuel (pouces levés/baissés)"

msgid "Visual training vs. rule-based filtering"
msgstr "Apprentissage visuel vs filtrage basé sur des règles"

msgid "Want more CLI features?"
msgstr "Vous voulez plus de fonctionnalités en ligne de commande ?"

msgid "Want more MCP features?"
msgstr "Envie de plus de fonctionnalités MCP ?"

msgid "Warren Robinett wrote a BASIC interpreter in 64 bytes of RAM. Max 9 lines, 64 symbols, integers 0&ndash;99."
msgstr ""
"Warren Robinett a écrit un interpréteur BASIC dans 64 octets de RAM. Maximum : 9 lignes, 64 symboles, "
"entiers de 0&ndash;99."

msgid ""
"Washington State bill HB2320 would require 3D printers to phone home and refuse to print known firearms. "
"Why it's technically infeasible."
msgstr ""
"Le projet de loi HB2320 de l’État de Washington obligerait les imprimantes 3D à appeler leur fabricant et à"
" refuser d’imprimer des armes à feu connues. Pourquoi cela est techniquement irréalisable."

msgid "We accept all major credit cards via Stripe (Visa, Mastercard, American Express, Discover) and PayPal."
msgstr ""
"Nous acceptons toutes les principales cartes de crédit via Stripe (Visa, Mastercard, American Express, "
"Discover) ainsi que PayPal."

msgid ""
"We love pull requests. If you want to add an endpoint, modify output, or make something better, <a "
"href=\"http://github.com/samuelclay/NewsBlur\">NewsBlur's repo on Github</a> is the place to make that "
"happen."
msgstr ""
"Nous adorons les pull requests. Si vous souhaitez ajouter un point de terminaison, modifier la sortie ou "
"améliorer quelque chose, le dépôt Github de <a href=\"http://github.com/samuelclay/NewsBlur\">NewsBlur est "
"l’endroit idéal pour le faire.</a>"

msgid ""
"We reserve the right to revise these guidelines. If you violate the spirit of these terms, expect to be "
"blocked without advance warning."
msgstr ""
"Nous nous réservons le droit de modifier ces règles. Si vous enfreignez l’esprit de ces conditions, vous "
"risquez d’être bloqué sans avertissement préalable."

#, python-format
msgid ""
"We're quite pleased to point out that this entire API is open-source, including the implementation of the "
"endpoints. You can find the source of the <a "
"href=\"http://github.com/samuelclay/NewsBlur/tree/master/apps/reader/views.py\">%(reader_path)s views "
"source</a>, <a "
"href=\"http://github.com/samuelclay/NewsBlur/tree/master/apps/social/views.py\">%(social_path)s views "
"source</a>, <a "
"href=\"http://github.com/samuelclay/NewsBlur/tree/master/apps/rss_feeds/views.py\">%(feeds_path)s views "
"source</a>, as well as <a "
"href=\"http://github.com/samuelclay/NewsBlur/tree/master/templates/static/api.yml\">the API definitions in "
"YAML</a>."
msgstr ""
"Nous sommes ravis de souligner que cette API est entièrement open source, y compris l’implémentation des "
"points de terminaison. Vous trouverez le code source des vues <a "
"href=\"http://github.com/samuelclay/NewsBlur/tree/master/apps/reader/views.py\">%(reader_path)s source des "
"vues</a>, <a "
"href=\"http://github.com/samuelclay/NewsBlur/tree/master/apps/social/views.py\">%(social_path)s source des "
"vues</a>, <a "
"href=\"http://github.com/samuelclay/NewsBlur/tree/master/apps/rss_feeds/views.py\">%(feeds_path)s source "
"des vues</a>, ainsi que <a "
"href=\"http://github.com/samuelclay/NewsBlur/tree/master/templates/static/api.yml\">les définitions de "
"l’API en YAML</a>."

